5. Apply a color threshold to the hue channel to isolate the sunset colors.
6. Combine the thresholded hue and value channels to create a binary mask.
7. Apply the binary mask to the original RGB image to create a color-enhanced image.
To incorporate image stabilization techniques to remove any motion blur present in the image, we can use the `imregtform` function to estimate the transformation required to align the image with a reference image. We can then use the `imwarp` function to apply the transformation to the image.
