Yes, you can use MATLAB code to accomplish this task. One way to do this is to use natural language processing (NLP) techniques to parse the text and identify the adjectives and adverbs in each sentence. Here's a rough outline of how you could approach this:
1. Load the text into MATLAB as a string.
2. Use a natural language processing toolkit, such as the Stanford NLP toolkit or NLTK, to tokenize the text into sentences.
3. For each sentence, use the same NLP toolkit to identify the adjectives and adverbs.
4. Check if each sentence contains at least one adjective and one adverb. If not, flag the sentence as missing one or both of these parts of speech.
5. Repeat for all sentences in the text.
Here's some sample MATLAB code to get you started:
```matlab
% Load the text into MATLAB as a string
text = 'Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. Sed blandit libero vel justo malesuada, non lobortis nulla bibendum. Nulla facilisi.';
% Use the Stanford NLP toolkit to tokenize the text into sentences
javaaddpath('stanford-corenlp-full-2018-10-05/stanford-corenlp-3.9.2.jar');
javaaddpath('stanford-corenlp-full-2018-10-05/stanford-corenlp-3.9.2-models.jar');
props = java.util.Properties();
props.setProperty('annotators', 'tokenize, ssplit');
pipeline = edu.stanford.nlp.pipeline.StanfordCoreNLP(props);
document = edu.stanford.nlp.pipeline.CoreDocument(text);
pipeline.annotate(document);
sentences = document.sentences();
% Loop through each sentence and check for adjectives and adverbs
for i = 1:length(sentences)
    sentence = sentences(i);
    sentence_text = sentence.text();

    % Use the Stanford NLP toolkit to identify adjectives and adverbs
    props.setProperty('annotators', 'tokenize, ssplit, pos');
    pipeline = edu.stanford.nlp.pipeline.StanfordCoreNLP(props);
    document = edu.stanford.nlp.pipeline.CoreDocument(sentence_text);
    pipeline.annotate(document);
    words = document.tokens();
    adjectives = {};
    adverbs = {};
    for j = 1:length(words)
        word = words(j);
        pos_tag = word.get(CoreAnnotations.PartOfSpeechAnnotation.class);
        if strcmp(pos_tag, 'JJ')
            adjectives{end+1} = word.word();
        elseif strcmp(pos_tag, 'RB')
            adverbs{end+1} = word.word();
        end
    end

    % Check if the sentence contains at least one adjective and one adverb
    if isempty(adjectives) || isempty(adverbs)
        fprintf('Sentence "%s" is missing either an adjective or an adverb.\n', sentence_text);
    end
end
```
Note that this code assumes you have downloaded and installed the Stanford NLP toolkit and included the necessary JAR files in your MATLAB environment. You'll also need to modify the path to the JAR files to match your local setup.

