Here is an example using Accord.NET:
```
using System;
using Accord.Math;
using Accord.Statistics.Models.Regression;
namespace LatentVariableModel
{
    class Program
    {
        static void Main(string[] args)
        {
            int n = 100; // number of data points
            int k = 2; // number of latent variables
            // generate some data
            double[][] x = new double[n][];
            double[] y = new double[n];
            for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)
            {
                x[i] = new double[k];
                for (int j = 0; j < k; j++)
                {
                    x[i][j] = Accord.Statistics.Distributions.Univariate.Normal(0, 1).Generate();
                }
                y[i] = x[i][0] + x[i][1] + Accord.Statistics.Distributions.Univariate.Normal(0, 0.1).Generate();
            }
            // create model
            var model = new MultivariateLinearRegression(k);
            // fit model to data
            model.Regress(x, y);
            // get coefficients
            double[] coefficients = model.Coefficients;
            Console.WriteLine(coefficients.ToVectorString());
            // make predictions
            double[][] xTest = new double[10][];
            for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++)
            {
                xTest[i] = new double[k];
                for (int j = 0; j < k; j++)
                {
                    xTest[i][j] = Accord.Statistics.Distributions.Univariate.Normal(0, 1).Generate();
                }
            }
            double[] yTest = model.Transform(xTest);
            Console.WriteLine(yTest.ToVectorString());
        }
    }
}
```
This code implements a linear regression model with two latent variables using Accord.NET. It generates some data, fits the model to the data, and makes predictions on new data. The `MultivariateLinearRegression` class represents the linear regression model, and is fit to the data using the `Regress` method. The `coefficients` variable represents the coefficients of the linear model. The `Transform` method is used to make predictions on new data. The output of the program is the inferred values of `coefficients` and the predicted values of `yTest`.

