I want to analyze each person's motivation and determine what factor(s) influenced their decision. Can you provide a sample C# code that would help me achieve this task?

output:
Yes, I can help you with that. Here's a sample C# code that you can use to analyze the dataset and determine the dominant factor influencing each person's decision:
```
using System;
using Newtonsoft.Json;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.Linq;
namespace DecisionAnalysis
{
    class Program
    {
        static void Main(string[] args)
        {
            string jsonData = @"
            {
              ""responses"": [
                {
                  ""id"": 1,
                  ""option"": ""Option A"",
                  ""motivation"": ""Peer pressure from colleagues who chose Option A""
                },
                {
                  ""id"": 2,
                  ""option"": ""Option B"",
                  ""motivation"": ""Personal preference for Option B""
                },
                {
                  ""id"": 3,
                  ""option"": ""Option A"",
                  ""motivation"": ""Desire to try something new""
                },
                {
                  ""id"": 4,
                  ""option"": ""Option B"",
                  ""motivation"": ""Better value for money""
                },
                {
                  ""id"": 5,
                  ""option"": ""Option A"",
                  ""motivation"": ""Recommendation from a trusted friend""
                },
                {
                  ""id"": 6,
                  ""option"": ""Option B"",
                  ""motivation"": ""Previous positive experience with Option B""
                },
                {
                  ""id"": 7,
                  ""option"": ""Option A"",
                  ""motivation"": ""Influence of advertising""
                },
                {
                  ""id"": 8,
                  ""option"": ""Option B"",
                  ""motivation"": ""Availability of Option B""
                },
                {
                  ""id"": 9,
                  ""option"": ""Option A"",
                  ""motivation"": ""Desire to stand out from the crowd""
                },
                {
                  ""id"": 10,
                  ""option"": ""Option B"",
                  ""motivation"": ""Influence of a celebrity endorsement""
                }
              ]
            }";
            // Deserialize JSON data into a list of responses
            var responses = JsonConvert.DeserializeObject<ResponseList>(jsonData);
            // Group responses by option chosen
            var groupedResponses = responses.Responses.GroupBy(r => r.Option);
            foreach (var group in groupedResponses)
            {
                Console.WriteLine($"Option {group.Key}:");
                // Get list of motivations for this option
                var motivations = group.Select(r => r.Motivation);
                // Count occurrences of each motivation
                var motivationCounts = CountMotivations(motivations);
                // Determine dominant motivation(s)
                var dominantMotivations = GetDominantMotivations(motivationCounts);
                Console.WriteLine($"Dominant motivation(s): {string.Join(", ", dominantMotivations)}\n");
            }
            Console.ReadLine();
        }
        static Dictionary<string, int> CountMotivations(IEnumerable<string> motivations)
        {
            var counts = new Dictionary<string, int>();
            foreach (var motivation in motivations)
            {
                if (counts.ContainsKey(motivation))
                {
                    counts[motivation]++;
                }
                else
                {
                    counts[motivation] = 1;
                }
            }
            return counts;
        }
        static List<string> GetDominantMotivations(Dictionary<string, int> motivationCounts)
        {
            var maxCount = motivationCounts.Values.Max();
            return motivationCounts.Where(m => m.Value == maxCount).Select(m => m.Key).ToList();
        }
    }
    class ResponseList
    {
        public List<Response> Responses { get; set; }
    }
    class Response
    {
        public int Id { get; set; }
        public string Option { get; set; }
        public string Motivation { get; set; }
    }
}
```
This code first deserializes the JSON data into a list of `Response` objects. It then groups the responses by the option chosen, and for each option, it counts the occurrences of each motivation and determines the dominant motivation(s). The `CountMotivations` method counts the occurrences of each motivation, and the `GetDominantMotivations` method determines the dominant motivation(s).
