How can I extract the sum of even numbers and the product of odd numbers in a given string of alphanumeric characters using PHP?
Consider this string: "a2b3c4d5e6f7g8h9i1j". We can treat 'a' as 1, 'b' as 2 and so on, up to 'j' as 10.
Here's a PHP code that can solve this problem:
$string = "a2b3c4d5e6f7g8h9i1j";
$even_sum = 0;
$odd_product = 1;
for ($i = 0; $i < strlen($string); $i++) {
  if (ctype_alpha($string[$i])) {
    $num = ord(strtolower($string[$i])) - 96;
  } else {
    $num = intval($string[$i]);
  }

  if ($num % 2 == 0) {
    $even_sum += $num;
  } else {
    $odd_product *= $num;
  }
}
echo "Sum of even numbers: " . $even_sum . "<br>";
echo "Product of odd numbers: " . $odd_product . "<br>";

